Mattocks are the most powerful, but I prefer others because mattocks are 
heavy, two handed, and have the minus to hit (not much of an issue, I 
know). I find it annoying when I have autodig on, too.

I would say get your hands on a silver saber. The best artifact for 
archaeologists is easily Grayswandir, and I like it one handed (though 
it doesn't help if you're spellcasting anyway). Silver sabers are 
excellent weapons in general; you end up fighting a LOT of silver hating 
creatures.

> Concerning the spell power - just read some of the spellbooks, since
> Archeologists are really good spellcasters in the late mid to endgame.
> 
